  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the first step protonation of alcohol takes place which leads to the formation of carbocation. Ring expansion takes place in the next step. In the given process five membered ring&nbsp;become six membered ring. Now, the carbocation loses proton in the presence of potassium hydroxide to give alkene.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d1843ca9-36f0-4d42-80a1-91fe5bc5640c.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 490px;\" /></p>",
